complexity: time=O(log n) | space=O(1)
complexity_note: n is the number n. Count `math.gcd` as O(1).
why_time: The answer is at most n × min(a, b, c), so the guessing game makes about log₂ of that many guesses, and each count is a formula: O(log n).
why_space: A few numbers.
hint: The multiples of a up to x number `x // a`. Adding the counts for a, b and c counts the multiples of two of them twice, so take away `x // lcm(a, b)` and the same for the other two pairs. That takes away the multiples of all three once too often, so add back `x // lcm(a, b, c)`.
hint: The lowest common multiple is `lcm(x, y) = x * y // math.gcd(x, y)`, and the lowest common multiple of all three is `lcm(lcm(a, b), c)`.
